# Normalise to LF in the repository. Without this, a Windows checkout writes
# CRLF into shell scripts, and a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter named "/bin/sh\r". The container then fails to start with a
# "no such file or directory" that names a file which plainly exists.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish files that must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
